[
  [
    "text 54.00 72.98 18 \"The Articles\"",
    "text 54.00 90.80 11 \"When this inventory was read over to the emperor, he directed me, although in\"",
    "text 54.00 106.20 11 \"very gentle terms, to deliver up the several particulars:\"",
    "text 64.47 127.10 11 \"• \"",
    "text 70.50 127.10 11 \"my scimitar, scabbard and all\"",
    "text 64.47 142.50 11 \"• \"",
    "text 70.50 142.50 11 \"my pocket pistols\"",
    "text 64.47 157.90 11 \"• \"",
    "text 70.50 157.90 11 \"my pouch of powder and bullets\"",
    "text 64.47 173.30 11 \"• \"",
    "text 70.50 173.30 11 \"my watch, my purse, and my knife and razor\"",
    "text 54.00 194.20 11 \"These articles were brought to me by Skyresh Bolgolam in person, and the first\"",
    "text 54.00 209.60 11 \"of them read as follows:\"",
    "text 60.49 230.50 11 \"1. \"",
    "text 70.50 230.50 11 \"The man-mountain shall not depart from our dominions, without our\"",
    "text 70.50 245.90 11 \"license under our great seal.\"",
    "text 60.49 266.80 11 \"2. \"",
    "text 70.50 266.80 11 \"He shall not presume to come into our metropolis, without our express\"",
    "text 70.50 282.20 11 \"order; at which time, the inhabitants shall have two hours warning to keep\"",
    "text 70.50 297.60 11 \"within doors.\"",
    "text 70.50 318.50 11 \"The said man-mountain shall confine his walks to our principal high roads,\"",
    "text 70.50 333.90 11 \"and not offer to walk, or lie down, in a meadow or field of corn.\"",
    "text 54.00 354.80 11 \"The searchers had gone through every pocket about me, and in each of them\"",
    "text 54.00 370.20 11 \"they found something:\"",
    "text 64.47 391.10 11 \"• \"",
    "text 70.50 391.10 11 \"In the right coat-pocket\"",
    "text 81.39 406.50 11 \"◦ \"",
    "text 87.00 406.50 11 \"one great piece of coarse-cloth, large enough to be a foot-cloth\"",
    "text 64.47 421.90 11 \"• \"",
    "text 70.50 421.90 11 \"In the left pocket\"",
    "text 81.39 437.30 11 \"◦ \"",
    "text 87.00 437.30 11 \"a huge silver chest, with a cover of the same metal\"",
    "text 81.39 452.70 11 \"◦ \"",
    "text 87.00 452.70 11 \"a sort of dust, which set them both a sneezing\"",
    "text 54.00 473.60 11 \"The last of the articles bound me to the service of the emperor:\""
  ],
  [
    "text 48.49 65.60 11 \"7. \"",
    "text 58.50 65.60 11 \"That the said man-mountain shall, at his times of leisure, be aiding and\"",
    "text 58.50 81.00 11 \"assisting to our workmen, in helping to raise certain great stones, towards\"",
    "text 58.50 96.40 11 \"covering the wall of the principal park.\"",
    "text 48.49 111.80 11 \"8. \"",
    "text 58.50 111.80 11 \"That the said man-mountain shall, in two moons' time, deliver in an exact\"",
    "text 58.50 127.20 11 \"survey of the circumference of our dominions, by a computation of his own\"",
    "text 58.50 142.60 11 \"paces round the coast.\"",
    "text 48.49 158.00 11 \"9. \"",
    "text 58.50 158.00 11 \"That, upon his solemn oath to observe all the above articles, the said man-\"",
    "text 58.50 173.40 11 \"mountain shall have a daily allowance of meat and drink sufficient for the\"",
    "text 58.50 188.80 11 \"support of 1724 of our subjects.\"",
    "text 42.00 209.70 11 \"I swore and subscribed to these articles with great cheerfulness and content,\"",
    "text 42.00 225.10 11 \"although some of them were not so honourable as I could have wished.\"",
    "text 213.84 624.19 9 \"2\""
  ]
]
